{"ld": 2216, "paper": "SP903", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Establish the Maine Blue Economy Center", "sponsor_id": "s-curry-glenn", "cosponsor_ids": [], "committee_code": "HED", "committee_name": "Housing and Economic Development", "summary": {"text": "This bill is reported out by the Joint Standing Committee on Housing and Economic Development pursuant to Resolve 2025, chapter 114. The bill establishes the Maine Blue Economy Center as a body corporate and politic and a public instrumentality of the State 2106 to leverage and expand the State's blue economy sector. The bill requires the center to 2117 submit an interim report upon appointment of all members of the center's board of directors 2128 and appropriates $1,000,000 in one-time funds in fiscal year 2026-27 for the center's start- 2139 up costs.\n\nThe committee has not taken a position on the substance of this bill. By reporting this bill out, the committee is not suggesting and does not intend to suggest that it agrees or disagrees with any aspect of this bill. The committee is reporting the bill out for the sole purpose of having a bill printed that can be referred to the committee for an appropriate public hearing and subsequent processing in the normal course. The committee is taking this action to ensure clarity and transparency in the legislative review of the proposals contained in the bill.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0903&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Enacted", "final_disposition": {"label": "Enacted", "date": "2026-04-16", "governor_action": "Signed", "governor_action_date": "2026-04-16"}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 2216)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0903&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (S-637)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0903&item=